Breaking it down

Endpoints = URLs
• /data
• /data/{id}

Methods = action type
• GET    → retrieve
• POST   → create
• PUT    → modify
• DELETE → remove

Storage layer (very important)
• items = []
• lives only in RAM
• resets when server restarts

--------------------------------------------------

Key architecture idea

Right now your system is:

• Stateless API layer (FastAPI)
• Temporary state layer (Python list)

No database means:
• No persistence
• No history
• No recovery after restart

--------------------------------------------------

Final mental model

• Endpoint = “WHERE”
• HTTP method = “WHAT ACTION”
• Function = “HOW IT HAPPENS”
• items = “TEMPORARY MEMORY”

Flow:

Client
 → chooses endpoint + method
 → sends request
 → FastAPI routes it
 → Python function runs
 → modifies or reads items
 → returns JSON response
